\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 11,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "a person accused of an offence punishable with imprisonment for a term which may be less than seven years or which may extend to seven years with or without fine, cannot be arrested by the police officer only on his satisfaction",\u8232 "reason": "It directly states that, for qualifying offences, merely believing the accused committed the offence is insufficient and additional arrest necessity is required.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 12,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "All the State Governments to instruct its police officers not to automatically arrest when a case under Section 498-A of the IPC is registered",\u8232 "reason": "It directly answers the question by expressly prohibiting automatic arrest upon registration of a 498A case and requiring satisfaction of Section 41 parameters.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 13,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "All the State Governments to instruct its police officers not to automatically arrest when a case under Section 498-A of the IPC is registered",\u8232 "reason": "It expressly states that police must not automatically arrest after 498A registration and instead must assess necessity under Section 41.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 14,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "After registration of the case on 3.6.1999, the investigating officer recorded the statements of witnesses under Section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.",\u8232 "reason": "It mentions a registered 498A case and subsequent proceedings, but does not state the governing rule against automatic arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 15,\u8232 "mark": "No",\u8232 "evidence": "Consequences of cruelty which are likely to drive a woman to commit suicide or to cause grave injury or danger to life, limb or health",\u8232 "reason": "It addresses the substantive elements of cruelty under Section 498A, not whether police may automatically arrest after registering a case.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 16,\u8232 "mark": "No",\u8232 "evidence": "It must be borne in mind that all these provisions relate to cognizance of the offence by the court.",\u8232 "reason": "It concerns court cognizance and procedural provisions for Section 498A, not the legality or necessity of automatic police arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \}\u8232 ],\u8232 "good_answer_present": "Yes",\u8232 "best_passage_no": 12,\u8232 "caveats": ""\u8232 \}\
